  "edinburgh-heart-of-scotland": {
    "id": "edinburgh-heart-of-scotland",
    "service": "luxury-tours",
    "duration": "Three Days",
    "title": "Edinburgh and the Heart of Scotland",
    "story": [
      "Three days is enough to understand why Scotland's story is told the way it is. It begins in a capital built in two halves: the medieval Old Town, all closes and wynds on its ridge, and the Georgian New Town laid out below it by a 26-year-old architect who won the competition in 1766.",
      "From there the road runs north to Stirling, the hinge of the country's history. Wallace fought below its castle in 1297, and Bruce won at Bannockburn in sight of it in 1314. Beyond lie the Trossachs and Loch Lomond, Rob Roy's country, which Walter Scott's novel made famous in 1817."
    ],
    "start": {
      "name": "Edinburgh Airport",
      "lon": -3.37,
      "lat": 55.95,
      "label": "left"
    },
    "days": [
      {
        "title": "Edinburgh",
        "highlights": [
          "Met at the airport and settled into the heart of the Old Town",
          "An afternoon in the closes and wynds with a guide who knows the stories the crowds walk past",
          "An evening at the castle, then dinner at one of the city's finest tables"
        ],
        "onTheRoad": "In 1828 Burke and Hare murdered sixteen people within a short walk of here and sold them to an anatomist. Their crimes gave the language the word \"burking\".",
        "stops": [
          {
            "name": "Edinburgh",
            "lon": -3.19,
            "lat": 55.95
          }
        ],
        "route": [
          [-3.369, 55.948],
