  "grand-sweep": {
    "id": "grand-sweep",
    "service": "luxury-tours",
    "duration": "Seven Days",
    "title": "The Grand Sweep, South to Far North",
    "story": [
      "A week from the capital to the empty roads of the far north is the journey people take once and remember for good. It follows roads first built by soldiers: General Wade laid some 240 miles of military road after the 1715 rising to hold the Highlands down. Today the same country is the most open space in Britain.",
      "It passes through the history that shaped the north. The Jacobites rose and fell here, and within a lifetime of Culloden came the Clearances, which emptied whole glens. Then, in Speyside, it ends with a happier story: the whisky smugglers who went legal."
    ],
